{"step_index":11076,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T14:30:07Z","thinking":"Data points are recorded approximately every 2 to 2.5 seconds, as the timestamps indicate. This equates to roughly 25 to 30 data points per minute. This interval needs to be considered when calculating averages or trends over time. Further investigation is warranted to understand the implication of Iraq Bhai's statement.\n\n\nThe core principle is that historical data in the graph must remain static upon new data arrival; only the latest point should animate. This requires disabling all chart animations and ensuring a fixed Y-axis scale (0-100% for CPU/RAM).  When new data appears, update the existing last point if the timestamp matches or append a new point and shift the oldest point if the window size is exceeded. Highlighting the latest point can improve visual clarity.\n\n\n`08:30:00` Disabling chart animations and setting a fixed Y-axis (0-100%) are critical for stable real-time display. Ensuring chart updates are performed without any animation will preserve historical data integrity.  `08:30:10` The existing chart instance will be updated by assigning new data and explicitly disabling any form of animation on update. `08:30:20`  The Y-axis range is fixed to prevent rescaling, thereby avoiding any bouncing effect when new data arrives. `08:30:28` It's hypothesized that focusing updates on the latest point only will be more visually coherent.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport shutil\n\ndef format_size(size_bytes):\n    for unit in ['B', 'KB', 'MB', 'GB', 'TB']:\n        if size_bytes < 1024.0:\n            return f'{size_bytes:.2f} {unit}'\n        size_bytes /= 1024.0\n    return f'{size_bytes:.2f} PB'\n\ndef get_drive_info(mount_point, label, drive_letter):\n    total, used, free = shutil.disk_usage(mount_point)\n    pct = (used / total) * 100 if total > 0 else 0\n    return {\n        'letter': drive_letter,\n        'label': label,\n        'path': mount_point,\n        'total': total,\n        'total_str': format_size(total),\n        'used': used,\n        'used_str': format_size(used),\n        'free': free,\n        'free_str': format_size(free),\n        'percent': round(pct, 1)\n    }\n\nprint('C:', get_drive_info('/', 'Local Disk (C: OS Root)', 'C'))\nprint('D:', get_drive_info('/home', 'Data Disk (D: NVMe Home)', 'D'))\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing real drive calculations","toolSummary":"Calculate C: and D: stats"}}]}
